# Local development state. This repository documents a database that is meant to
# persist, so what lives here is either generated per machine or must never be shared.

# Credentials. dev/.env holds POSTGRES_PASSWORD and the per-role passwords generated
# by scripts/db/db. There is deliberately no committed copy of it, and no default that
# a developer might reuse against a real server.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
dev/.env
dev/.env.*
!dev/.env.example

# TLS material. init.sh keeps the private CA key and the server key in the afpc_tls
# docker volume, never on this checkout; the exported CA certificate (dev/tls/*.crt)
# is the public half and IS committed, because auditors need it for sslmode=verify-full.
*.key
*.pem
*.p12
*.pfx
dev/tls/*.key
dev/tls/*.csr
dev/tls/*.srl

# Database dumps: pg_dump output can contain customer PII.
backup/
*.dump
*.sql.gz

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
venv/
.venv/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
htmlcov/
.coverage
*.egg-info/

# Editors and OS
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Local scratch that agents in this project have historically written next to
# themselves. Anything under a name that implies throwaway should not be tracked.
tmp/
.cache/
*.log

# The JADA reference drop's archive, left at the repository root when it was unpacked into
# agents/jada/. The tree is what matters and it is untracked on purpose (see dev/README); the zip is
# neither, so it is ignored by name rather than deleted, because a download that has to be repeated is
# worse than one line here. A "(1)" suffix is a browser resolving a second download of the same file.
dumb_agent-jw_improvements*.zip

# agents/jada/ is the reference drop, and it is ignored rather than merely untracked. The difference is
# the point: untracked-but-not-ignored means `git add -A` sweeps a 16 MB vendored tree into the next
# commit, which is what happened the first time this directory was staged around - the intent was to
# commit the deployment and the index filled with files that are not deployment. Keeping it out of the
# index is the machine-readable form of the decision that the reference stays what it was when it
# arrived, unmodified and not this project's source. Read-only to the build user for the same reason.
agents/jada/

# Written by scripts/db/init.sh: the address the leaf certificate was just issued for, which is the only
# value AFPC_PG_HOST can take on this machine and is therefore not a guess to be committed. It names a
# private address on a specific network, and a cloned compose file that fell back to it would be pointing
# a stranger's browser and agent at somebody's LAN.
agents/customer_service/.env
